WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:06.770
Let's go next to our caller from the 3 1 4
area code caller from 3 1 4.

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:07.770
What's your name?

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:08.790
Where are you calling from?

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.809
Hello, David.

00:00:10.809 --> 00:00:18.650
This is Alan and I am calling from St. Charles,
Missouri.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:21.890
What's on your mind today, Alan?

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:23.890
I was.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:28.279
Wondering that if Hillary Clinton had been
the president.

00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:31.509
How do you think this whole covered?

00:00:31.509 --> 00:00:38.240
19 The pandemic was played out in America.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:44.510
It would still be a pandemic, but our response
would have been closer to what South Korea

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.660
did than what we have today.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:51.210
So as an example, Hillary Clinton would not
have become president.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:54.550
And in 2018 disbanded the pandemic response
team.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.010
She wouldn't have done that.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:01:02.870
Hillary Clinton would not have ignored the
color coded 69 page pandemic response playbook

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:08.190
that the Obama administration created after
Ebola and left behind.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:13.640
Hillary Clinton would not have had such administration
turnover over that.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:19.530
More than half of the people who were briefed
on pandemic response in 2017 by the Obama

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:23.840
administration would have already been fired
or resigned, as is the case with the Trump

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:24.840
administration.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:28.870
So can we say we would have been South Korea
with Hillary Clinton as president?

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:30.300
Of course not.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:35.890
But just on those three issues alone, we would
have been far better suited to deal with this

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:37.220
than we are under Donald Trump.

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:42.850
It's very easy to go up to try to rewrite
history or to have these alternative histories.

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:44.530
If this that the other thing.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:49.030
But there's no question that on just those
three points alone, we would have been so

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:54.700
much better off with Hillary Clinton running
this than Donald Trump.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:02:04.400
And I also wondered, you know, you think in
the long term after this has passed that we

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:13.629
will ever get back to the point of having
packed stadiums and sold out concerts with

00:02:13.629 --> 00:02:16.689
tens of thousands of people?

00:02:16.689 --> 00:02:17.730
You know, I think we will.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:18.870
I think we will.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:24.609
And part of the reason why I think that is
it it is common that it always feels like

00:02:24.609 --> 00:02:27.049
things will never go back to the way they
were.

00:02:27.049 --> 00:02:32.579
And in some ways, sometimes things don't like
things will always be a little different.

00:02:32.579 --> 00:02:34.799
But I believe it could take a while.

00:02:34.799 --> 00:02:40.040
But eventually we will get back to that, hopefully
with more precautions, better functioning

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:47.379
systems and more preparedness to deal with
this if it is not if but when it happens again.

00:02:47.379 --> 00:02:50.510
Kind of like after nine eleven.

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:51.510
Yes.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:52.510
Yes.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:56.269
It felt like it wouldn't, you know, flying
was never going to just be flying again.

00:02:56.269 --> 00:02:58.030
And you know, it it is different.

00:02:58.030 --> 00:02:59.329
We have the TSA now.

00:02:59.329 --> 00:03:00.329
We didn't before.

00:03:00.329 --> 00:03:01.989
It's not the same.

00:03:01.989 --> 00:03:06.780
But by and large, things do go back to mostly
to the way that that they were.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.709
Alan, thank you so much for the call.

00:03:08.709 --> 00:03:11.700
I so appreciate, appreciated and appreciate
the thoughtful question.

